<title>EGYPT: Egypt sets prices for cotton export.</title>
<headline>Egypt sets prices for cotton export.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian companies have set prices of between 224.00 and 100.00 centilibres (U.S. cents per lb) for the nine varieties and grades of cotton slated for export.</p>
<p>The prices are valid for one week, until midnight (2100 GMT) on Sunday, an official at the Alexandria Cotton Exporters Association told Reuters on Monday. The association coordinates exports by 11 state-owned firms and seven private sector ones.</p>
<p>The official said the amount of cotton they expect to export in the current year which began on September 1, was a high 125,000 to 150,000 tonnes, pushed up by the state's decision to let farmers export all varieties, including the valuable long-staple it diverted to the local textile industry.</p>
<p>The price ranges (all in centilibres) for the nine varities are:</p>
<p>	   FG/EX   FG+1/4   FG	FG-1/4   G/FG   G+3/8   G+1/4</p>
